  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nA dry cold frontal passage through early Friday will bring \ncooler near-normal temperatures and breezy winds. The \napproaching parent trough will keep our area in a southwest \nflow, keeping Saturday on the slightly warmer than normal side. \nBy late Saturday, the aforementioned trough will move inland and\nover our area as a closed upper low, returning chances of \nshowers/thunderstorms and gusty winds. This low passage will \nkeep Sunday cooler with precipitation chances remaining mainly \nover high terrain areas. A mostly dry longwave trough off the \nPacific will keep our area under a southwest flow early next \nweek. As such, Monday through Tuesday see a return of dry \nconditions and warmer temperatures.",
